       ],
       "changes": [
         "Map the bounded public System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary member subset with exact nominal interfaces and method flags.",
-        "Replace inline entry arrays and unsafe/ref helpers with managed reference-entry vectors and checked indexing; entries remain internal to collection operations. AC3.29 views capture them through an assembly-visible owned accessor, matching the existing cursor helper boundary.",
+        "Replace inline Entry arrays and unsafe/ref helpers with one managed storage owner containing hash, link, key and value columns. Checked ordinary arrays remove per-entry allocation while retaining captured storage identity across callbacks. Views capture storage through an assembly-visible owned accessor. ADR 0225 records the representation and measured tradeoffs.",
         "Use exact compiler-selected closed integer/value key operations instead of runtime reflection and EqualityComparer factory selection.",
         "Retain distinct value-key hash receiver semantics in FindValue and TryInsert.",
         "Compatibility batch 005 stores the supplied IEqualityComparer<TKey> and forwards hash/equality through ordinary managed dispatch. Null and exact owned value-default singleton comparers retain default KeyOperations receiver semantics; custom callbacks receive value copies. Remove the obsolete CreateOrdinal factories and their two construction grants.",
-        "AC3.3 adds Remove with/without out value and Clear; clear key/value payloads and reuse private entry slots. AC3.16 adds the capacity constructor; compatibility batch 005 adds both comparer constructor overloads for admitted keys/comparers.",
+        "AC3.3 adds Remove with/without out value and Clear; ADR 0225 clears removed payloads only when their exact shapes contain references, preserving freed scalar values observable through callbacks. Clear resets every used column slot. AC3.16 adds the capacity constructor; compatibility batch 005 adds both comparer constructor overloads for admitted keys/comparers.",
         "Preserve the public generic/nongeneric/serialization interface declarations; unimplemented members remain compile-time errors.",
         "Preserve per-dictionary view identity and tracing cycles; constructors use ordinary validation helpers. ContainsValue captures the entries vector and compares copied value receivers through existing exact equality selection. Other unimplemented equality/copy/enumerator paths remain diagnostic.",
         "AC4.3 adds the concrete nested Enumerator. Walk active slots with ordinary accessors, materialize the pair before storing current, reset current/end index, and update version only after successful new-key insertion (including free-slot reuse). Boxed interface factories/legacy members remain diagnostic.",
